{"nodes": [{"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_fill_limit_undecidable", "label": "FILL-LIMIT \u2014 the tower's limit is undecidable from admissibility alone", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Answers MC-33's three options: (C) certified-open is true and now proved, (B) settled in its counterexample branch, (A) answered in the negative. What decides L is the clause the exhibits lack by construction \u2014 a bound deriving from a law independent of the index. The existence of L is the law's; its value is the world's."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_morphism_admissibility", "label": "Morphism-admissibility (A.morph, Birkhoff 1940)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a70\u2013\u00a71", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A new coordinate is admissible iff its bounds are lattice morphisms of the stage below; joins and meets in a product of chains are componentwise, and projections commute with both, so each stage is a sublattice of its box and E = 0."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_tower_lambda_13", "label": "The tower \u039b\u2088\u2026\u039b\u2081\u2083 (199,130 cells, fill 0.4168%)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a72", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Rebuilt from tower-1.py; the closure instrument returns E = 0 at \u039b\u2088\u2013\u039b\u2081\u2081, reproducing R 249 before it is pointed at anything new."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_continuations_pqt", "label": "The three admissible continuations P, Q and T", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a73\u2013\u00a74", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "P gives L = 0.031146% > 0, Q gives L = 0, T approaches fill(\u039b\u2081\u2083) from below \u2014 and P and Q share the same fourteenth axis, so the fourteenth stage does not know which limit it is heading for. Six built stages could not fix the asymptotics and neither can any finite number."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_register_333_bracket", "label": "Register 333's bracket [0, 0.4168%), tight and right-open", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a70; \u00a73", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "0 is attained and fill(\u039b\u2081\u2083) is the unattained supremum, because the book's own law makes the fourteenth ratio strictly below one."}, {"id": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_pipe_truncation_self_correction", "label": "Self-correction: the head-truncated first run", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a76", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Piping fill_limit.py through head closed the pipe at sixty lines and killed the process mid-segment, truncating the results file at \u039b\u2088; rerun to file, no figure changed, and it is registered here rather than hidden."}], "edges": [{"source": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_fill_limit_undecidable", "target": "drive_the_method_materials_fill_limit_finding_morphism_admissibility", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "drive/The Method Materials/FILL-LIMIT-FINDING.md", "source_location": "\u00a70", "weight": 1.0}, {"source":